==Strategy==
The main problem in this stage is the peons. You'll need a few [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] to kill large amounts of them at once, as well as something that can snipe Wahwah from a distance. Easy examples of peon clearers include [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], due to high cash flow, [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]], and any other Area Attack Cat. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] helps a lot in both killing most oncoming peons as well as chipping down Wahwah with its extreme [[Wave Attack]] damage. A different unit that can be used to chip down Wahwah is [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], especially with his Slow [[Talents|Talent]] leveled up, but it requires Cyberpunk Cat to stand behind the [[Cat Base]]. King Wahwah's Omni Strike causes him to stand 1,000 range away from the base, leaving him unable to hit Cyberpunk Cat. When Cyberpunk Cat knocks back Wahwah, his slow will render him immobile for a little while.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: A good meatshield here as he is able to tank many hits from the peons and especially Mr. Angel due to his [[Resistant|resistance]] to [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]].
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]: Viable option here, its Wave Attacks are able to deal high damage to oncoming peons and can deal decent damage to Wahwah.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]]: A great option here, as its insanely high Wave Attack damage can clear upcoming peons and knockback Wahwah, allowing you to gain ground.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]: Can be used to recieve more money from peons like Kroxo or Mr. Angel, and can deal enough damage to knockback Wahwah.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: If his [[Explosion]] Talent is unlocked, he can wipe out an entire wave of peons, as well as deal very high damage to Wahwah.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Used to crowd-control Wahwah and allow you to deal with the peons individually instead of dealing with both. He can also deal enough damage to knock him back occasionally, allowing you to regain ground.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]]/[[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] units work well here, as the EPICFEST units are built to deal with [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless enemies]] and the UBERFEST units tend to have high or decent area damage. [[Dark Aegis Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Aegis Garu]] in particular is an extremely helpful Uber for this stage, as his large health, resistance to Traitless enemies AND guaranteed Survive allows him to tank dozens of hits from King Wahwah.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Can be used to deal with the Brollows and is [[Immune to Knockback]], preventing your units from losing ground.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Can also be used a secondary rusher with Awakened Bahamut Cat to deal high damage to Wahwah if timed right.

